    "overviewDetail": "The British Virgin Islands (BVI) is one of the worldΓÇÖs most prominent offshore financial centres, widely recognised for its tax-neutral regime, efficient incorporation processes, and flexible corporate structures. It is a preferred jurisdiction for holding companies, investment vehicles, and international business operations.\n\nThe most commonly used entity is the Business Company (BC), which allows 100% foreign ownership and can be incorporated quickly with minimal capital requirements. The jurisdiction imposes no corporate income tax, capital gains tax, or withholding tax on companies conducting business outside the territory. This makes it highly attractive for cross-border structuring and asset protection.\n\nThe BVI Financial Services Commission (FSC) regulates the sector, ensuring compliance with international standards such as those set by the OECD and FATF. In recent years, the jurisdiction has strengthened its regulatory framework, including economic substance requirements and beneficial ownership reporting, to enhance transparency and maintain its global credibility.\n\nWith a stable legal system based on English common law, a well-established financial services ecosystem, and ongoing regulatory evolution, the British Virgin Islands continues to be a leading choice for global investors and businesses seeking efficient offshore structures.\n",
