    "FAQs": [
      {
        "id": 11,
        "question": "What is a BVI Business Company (BC)?",
        "answer": "A BC is the most common entity type in the BVI, used for international business, holding structures, and investment activities."
      },
      {
        "id": 10,
        "question": "Is the BVI a tax-free jurisdiction?",
        "answer": "Yes, BVI companies are generally exempt from corporate income tax, capital gains tax, and withholding tax on offshore activities."
      },
      {
        "id": 13,
        "question": "Is the BVI compliant with international regulations?",
        "answer": "Yes, the jurisdiction follows OECD and FATF standards, including economic substance and transparency requirements."
      },
      {
        "id": 12,
        "question": "Who regulates companies in the BVI?",
        "answer": "The BVI Financial Services Commission (FSC) oversees company registration and financial services regulation."
      },
      {
        "id": 14,
        "question": "How long does it take to set up a company?",
        "answer": "Incorporation is typically completed within 1ΓÇô3 business days, depending on documentation and service providers.\n"
